Everything is implemented and verified. Here's what changed:

**`app/auth.py`** — `require_api_key` now reads `X-API-Key`, looks it up in `VALID_API_KEYS`, and raises 401 with a specific message if missing or invalid. Returns the mapped username on success.

**`app/main.py`** — six changes total:

| Route | Method | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `GET /tasks` | `list_tasks` | Added optional `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` filters (combinable). Added `page` (default 1), `page_size` (default 20) pagination. |
| `POST /tasks` | `create_task` | Requires auth via `Depends(require_api_key)`. Validates `project_id` exists (404 if not). Auto-generates integer ID via `max(tasks, ...) + 1`. Returns 201 + the task. |
| `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` | `update_task` | Requires auth. Applies partial updates (`title`, `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to`). Returns 404 if not found. |
| `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` | `delete_task` | Requires auth. Returns 204 on success, 404 if not found. |

All 11 integration tests passed: filter by status, filter by priority, pagination, combined filters, create with/without auth, bad project ID, update, update-not-found, delete, delete-not-found.
